# Backend Standards

See `docs/12-backend-architecture.md` and `docs/18-coding-standards.md`.

## Structure

- One NestJS module per domain (`Auth`, `Users`, `Questions`, etc.).
- Controllers: HTTP mapping only; no business rules.
- Services: domain logic and orchestration.
- Repositories: Prisma access when abstraction aids testing; avoid empty wrappers.
- DTOs validated at the boundary; reject unknown fields.

## Data & migrations

- Prisma migrations are the only production schema path. Never `db push` in prod.
- Multi-row business operations use transactions.
- Soft-delete only where the schema documents it.

## Access control

- Use guards for auth + RBAC on every protected route.
- Answer/explanation fields stripped or omitted via a dedicated access-control service — never rely on the client.
- Check resource ownership for user-scoped mutations (bookmarks, profile, sessions).

## Jobs

- Enqueue via BullMQ only for async/long work (email, PDF processing, aggregations, cleanup).
- Jobs must be idempotent. Do not use queues for simple CRUD.

## API

- Version under `/api/v1`.
- Consistent success/error envelopes.
- Document with Swagger.
- Prefer cursor pagination for large question lists.
